Measure the cost of building a 200,000-item sequence three ways and explain the timings:

```python
import time
from collections import deque

def timed(fn):
    t = time.perf_counter(); fn(); return round(time.perf_counter() - t, 3)

n = 200_000
def front_list():
    a = []
    for i in range(n): a.insert(0, i)
def back_list():
    a = []
    for i in range(n): a.append(i)
def front_deque():
    d = deque()
    for i in range(n): d.appendleft(i)

print(timed(front_list), timed(back_list), timed(front_deque))
```

Then write a minimal doubly linked list with sentinel nodes and an O(1) `remove(node)` method.

